new file mode 100644
index 0000000..00c121f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/CAPTURE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+# Voice capture
+
+Talk into your iPhone. The server transcribes with Whisper, Claude splits what you said
+into tasks, notes and expenses, and each lands in a plain file you can open anywhere.
+
+```
+iPhone Shortcut -> POST /capture -> Whisper -> Claude -> DATA_DIR/capture/
+                                                          tasks.md
+                                                          notes.md
+                                                          expenses.csv
+                                                          inbox.md          (could not sort)
+                                                          transcripts.jsonl (every capture, raw)
+```
+
+## Server setup
+
+Add to `.env`, then restart:
+
+```
+ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
+CAPTURE_TOKEN=<output of: openssl rand -hex 32>
+CAPTURE_TOPICS=move,motorcycle,pj-shipping
+CAPTURE_DEFAULT_CURRENCY=MYR
+```
+
+`/capture` is the only endpoint on this server that checks a token. With `CAPTURE_TOKEN`
+empty it refuses every request. The other endpoints are still open to anyone who can reach
+the port, so keep the server on your LAN or Tailnet (see `HTTPS-TAILSCALE.md`), not on the
+public internet.
+
+Check it without a phone:
+
+```bash
+curl -s http://localhost:8000/capture \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $CAPTURE_TOKEN" \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"text": "paid 500 ringgit deposit for the bike, collect it Saturday"}'
+```
+
+## iPhone Shortcut
+
+Shortcuts app, new shortcut, four actions:
+
+1. **Record Audio**. Start: Immediately. Finish: On Tap.
+2. **Get Contents of URL**
+   - URL: `https://<your-server>/capture`
+   - Method: POST
+   - Headers: `Authorization` = `Bearer <CAPTURE_TOKEN>`
+   - Request Body: File, set to the Recorded Audio
+3. **Get Dictionary Value**. Get Value for `summary` in Contents of URL.
+4. **Show Notification** with the Dictionary Value.
+
+Put it on the Action Button or Back Tap. Text works too: send JSON `{"text": "..."}`.
+
+## What comes back
+
+```json
+{
+  "transcript": "paid 500 ringgit deposit for the bike collect it saturday",
+  "sorted": true,
+  "items": [
+    {"kind": "expense", "text": "Deposit for the bike", "amount": 500.0, "currency": "MYR", "due": null, "topic": "motorcycle"},
+    {"kind": "task", "text": "Collect the bike", "amount": null, "currency": null, "due": "2026-11-14", "topic": "motorcycle"}
+  ],
+  "error": null,
+  "summary": "Filed 1 task, 1 expense"
+}
+```
+
+If Claude is unreachable, the key is wrong, or it declines, you still get HTTP 200 with
+`"sorted": false`, the cause in `error`, and `summary` reading
+`Saved UNSORTED to inbox (...)`. The transcript is in `inbox.md` and `transcripts.jsonl`.
+Nothing is dropped.
+
+## Settings
+
+| Variable | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | none | Claude key. Unset means everything goes to the inbox. |
+| `CAPTURE_TOKEN` | none | Bearer token the Shortcut sends. Unset means 503. |
+| `CAPTURE_MODEL` | `claude-opus-5-5` | Any Claude model id. |
+| `CAPTURE_TOPICS` | empty | Comma-separated tags Claude may attach. |
+| `CAPTURE_DEFAULT_CURRENCY` | `MYR` | Used when you name an amount with no currency. |
